one burn scars, washes,\nslot canyons, and arroyos. Early estimates predict an area of 1 to 2\ninches of new rainfall for portions of southeast UT and southwest CO.\n\nThis is a preliminary forecast that hinges on slight shifts in a\nstrong moisture plume impacting the region. It also attempts to\ncapture the most statistically likely outcome, despite stronger and\nweaker outlier predictions. Outdoor enthusiasts, motorists, and\nresidents of recent flood impacted areas are encouraged to remain\nabreast of the developing forecast in the coming days.","ends":"2026-10-30T15:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; San Miguel, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8fb5d34f2d13ed8ac1ea289950d1e46b096a7bdd.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8fb5d34f2d13ed8ac1ea289950d1e46b096a7bdd.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-30T11:08:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 301108 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 508 AM MDT Fri Oct 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Precipitation chances return Friday PM with quick-hitting showers and storms for the lower elevations and flurries above 10,000 feet. - Another round of 1 to 3 inches of rain for parts of southeast Utah and Southwest Colorado is possible Sunday into Monday","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-30T06:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-302200- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1235 AM MDT Fri Oct 30 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&f